  "archived_at": "2026-11-14T07:39:34Z",
  "content_html": "<div class=\"twitter-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://x.com/nytimes/status/2120131200618545320?a=jkHWwIAeU5XIPlCBCnQ&amp;s=61&quot;,&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;Breaking News: Anthropic set a price range for its I.P.O. that values the A.I. company at up to $1.4 trillion, a staggering sum. &quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;nytimes&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;The New York Times&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/1098244578472280064/gjkVMelR_normal.png&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2026-11-10T12:27:23.000Z&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[],&quot;quoted_tweet&quot;:{},&quot;reply_count&quot;:24,&quot;retweet_count&quot;:21,&quot;like_count&quot;:91,&quot;impression_count&quot;:69692,&quot;expanded_url&quot;:{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://nyti.ms/4kHKc4X&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Anthropic Targets Valuation of Up to $1.4 Trillion for Blockbuster I.P.O.&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;The A.I. company&#8217;s pricing would make it one of the biggest ever public listings. It comes at a volatile moment amid fears that the A.I. boom may not be sustainable.&quot;,&quot;domain&quot;:&quot;nyti.ms&quot;,&quot;image&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/news_img/2120131203344826368/eI2agzh_?format=jpg&amp;name=orig&quot;},&quot;video_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_preview_media_key&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false}\" data-component-name=\"Twitter2ToDOM\"></div><p>After a bumbling start &#8230;</p><div class=\"twitter-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://x.com/stevekopack/status/2119979475957846382?a=9pcnErv9Fs0GSZrbPgM&amp;s=61&quot;,&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;(Reuters) - Anthropic sent out and then &#8204;retracted details of its blockbuster IPO filing, according to emails to bankers seen by Reuters late &#8288;on Monday.\\n\\n&quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;SteveKopack&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Steve Kopack&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/2097484389886103552/tn5ddEfw_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2026-11-10T02:24:29.000Z&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[],&quot;quoted_tweet&quot;:{},&quot;reply_count&quot;:5,&quot;retweet_count&quot;:7,&quot;like_count&quot;:37,&quot;impression_count&quot;:24244,&quot;expanded_url&quot;:{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.reuters.com/business/anthropic-aims-raise-up-693-billion-blockbuster-ipo-2026-11-10/&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;EXCLUSIVE: Anthropic aims to raise up to $69.3 billion in blockbuster IPO&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;Anthropic is &#8204;aiming to raise &#8203;as &#8203;much as $69.3 billion &#8288;in &#8203;what could &#8203;rank among the largest &#8203;initial &#8203;public offerings on &#8204;record, &#8288;according to a copy &#8203;of &#8203;a &#8288;filing seen &#8203;by &#8203;Reuters &#8288;on Monday.&quot;,&quot;domain&quot;:&quot;reuters.com&quot;,&quot;image&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/news_img/2119969758552760320/qp31_Knf?format=jpg&amp;name=orig&quot;},&quot;video_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_preview_media_key&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false}\" data-component-name=\"Twitter2ToDOM\"></div><p>&#8230; Anthropic just announced that it is  aiming to IPO at &#8220;up to&#8221; $1.4 trillion (more likely a bit less), an astronomical sum for a company that has (with the possible exception of one anomalous, heavily subsidized quarter) has never made a profit and that has nearly $900 billion in future liabilities. </p><div class=\"twitter-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://x.com/edzitron/status/2117673951623090662?a=6T_aPyJTSUxOmMBCeoo&amp;s=61&quot;,&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;Free newsletter: Anthropic's Q3 revenue growth slowed as costs exploded, and Ramp data shows Q4 growth decelerating by as much as 50%. With $895bn in commitments and a likely junk rating, both Anthropic and the AI industry face a future liquidity crisis.\\n&quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;edzitron&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Ed Zitron&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/2070326703281553408/ILxQjQF7_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2026-11-03T17:43:09.000Z&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[],&quot;quoted_tweet&quot;:{},&quot;reply_count&quot;:27,&quot;retweet_count&quot;:64,&quot;like_count&quot;:381,&quot;impression_count&quot;:74044,&quot;expanded_url&quot;:{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.wheresyoured.at/running-dry&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Running Dry&quot;,&quot;description&quot;:&quot;If you haven&#8217;t subscribed to Where&#8217;s Your Ed At, now&#8217;s the best time. I&#8217;ve extended the sale &#8212; 10% off of the $70-a-year subscription for life (click here!) &#8212; for new subscribers for another week. It&#8217;s a great way to support my work, and you&quot;,&quot;domain&quot;:&quot;wheresyoured.at&quot;,&quot;image&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/news_img/2117673952210243584/3OVQnsI2?format=jpg&amp;name=orig&quot;},&quot;video_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_preview_media_key&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false}\" data-component-name=\"Twitter2ToDOM\"></div><p>The Amended IPO itself is actually candid about the issues, to some degree:</p><div class=\"twitter-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://x.com/rdd147/status/2118782897893286154?a=xb1b1nxVLmVq6GgvuaM&amp;s=61&quot;,&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;Anthropic Ammended S-1\\n\\n&#8220;We expect our costs will increase over time and our losses will continue&#8221;\\n\\n&#8220;We do not expect our revenue will continue to grow at comparable rates&#8221;\\n\\nThis company has $110 billion in annual commitments that they admit they need to pay, but will need to&#8230;&quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;rdd147&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Roger&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/1974909490802851840/vfG-gO56_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;date&quot;:&quot;2026-11-06T19:09:42.000Z&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[],&quot;quoted_tweet&quot;:{&quot;full_text&quot;:&quot;OpenAI and Anthropic are absolutely going bankrupt if they don&#8217;t get out of these commitments. Getting out needs to be the priority before IPO. Anthropic itself admits in S1 the company will suffer potentially heavy losses speculating on early compute deals coming online faster https://t.co/vMsL7BDGBP&quot;,&quot;username&quot;:&quot;rdd147&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Roger&quot;,&quot;profile_image_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/profile_images/1974909490802851840/vfG-gO56_normal.jpg&quot;,&quot;photos&quot;:[{&quot;img_url&quot;:&quot;https://pbs.substack.com/media/HWdmL0taMAAqmPc.jpg&quot;,&quot;link_url&quot;:&quot;https://t.co/vMsL7BDGBP&quot;}]},&quot;reply_count&quot;:10,&quot;retweet_count&quot;:27,&quot;like_count&quot;:149,&quot;impression_count&quot;:12206,&quot;expanded_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_url&quot;:null,&quot;video_preview_media_key&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false}\" data-component-name=\"Twitter2ToDOM\"></div><p>The whole idea that they might be worth trillions mostly comes from projections like this absurd but popular one (try not to vomit when you look at the Y axis) made back in May, at the peak of the tokenmaxxing mania:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg\" width=\"1298\" height=\"1017\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:&quot;normal&quot;,&quot;height&quot;:1017,&quot;width&quot;:1298,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:0,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFAS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1f4b4c80-01af-4111-ae2d-b1ac52549b6b_1298x1017.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"></button><button class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\" tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\"></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>Predictions like that were predicated on the idea that Anthropic&#8217;s revenue would continue on the meteoric growth trajectory that tokenmaxxing drove.</p><p>The trouble is that it didn&#8217;t. </p><p>Quarter 2 growth was 147% compared to Q1, but Q3 wound up being a mere 47% compared to Q2. The decline of tokenmaxxing and the rise of good quality (if not quite top-tier) competitors from China began to take their toll. </p><p>A recent graph from TickerTrends (with a green line superimposed by me) makes it clear that the rocket has lost its zing: </p>\n      <p>\n          <a href=\"https://garymarcus.substack.com/p/just-say-no-to-anthropics-ipo\">\n              Read more\n          </a>\n      </p>",
